// One sweep, and the walk it is built on.
//
// The node store is in creation order and a function's own node is created
// last of all its nodes, so the nodes of function `f` are exactly the range
// from wherever the previous function ended through prog[f]. That gives every
// node an owner without a lookup per node -- node_fn scans the whole program
// list, which inside a sweep over every node would be quadratic.

// Returns the set's size *before* the sweep, so reach_mark stops when a sweep
// changes nothing.
reach_pass() {
  int n = len((import rfn));
  reach_funcs(0, 0);
} return int n;
